{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. And art Thou come with us to dwell,
\par Our Prince, our Guide, our Love, our Lord ?
\par And is Thy name Emmanuel,
\par God present with His world restored ? 
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The world is glad for Thee ! The rude
\par Wild moor, the city's crowded pen ;
\par Each waste, each people solitude,
\par Becomes a home for happy men.
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou bringest all again ; with Thee
\par Is light, is space, is breadth and room
\par For each thing fair, beloved, and free,
\par To have its hour of life and bloom.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Each heart's deep instinct unconfessed ;
\par Each lowly wish, each daring claim ;
\par All, all that life hath long repressed,
\par Unfolds, not fearing blight or blame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy reign eternal will not cease ;
\par Thy years are sure , and glad, and slow ;
\par Within Thy might world of peace 
\par The humblest flower hath leave to blow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Then come to heal Thy people's smart,
\par And with Thee bring Thy captive train ;
\par Come, Saviour of the world and heart,
\par Come, mighty victor over pain.\tab 
\par                                      Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

